= Federation (information technology) — Simple =

Federation in information technology is an arrangement in which independently administered systems interoperate through shared protocols, trust relationships, or exchange rules while retaining separate control.

Federated systems can share identity assertions, messages, content, or services without requiring one operator to own every participating system. Federation is therefore an architectural and governance relationship rather than a synonym for decentralization.

'''Important boundaries:'''
* federation ≠ decentralization
* federation ≠ single sign-on

